WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:08.937
This is Anthropic, Read Aloud. Today: Giving companies more control over their A I agents, with NVIDIA.

2
00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:14.156
Giving companies more control over their A I agents, with NVIDIA.

3
00:00:14.606 --> 00:00:18.866
From Claude Blog, published September 28, 2026.

4
00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:36.624
NVIDIA today announced the Open Agent Safety Platform, an open software platform and reference system design for strengthening A I security. Anthropic has collaborated with NVIDIA to bring additional layers of security and control to the agent stack.

5
00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:56.530
Claude Managed Agents, a suite of composable A P Is for building and deploying production-grade agents at scale, holds the credentials an agent needs in a vault so the agent never sees them. Open source NVIDIA OpenShell software is designed to control what the agent can execute and reach while it works.

6
00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:06.229
Customers who are using Managed Agents with OpenShell can limit what an agent can do, review what the agent did and confirm that the limits are in place.

7
00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:27.777
Companies are moving from using A I to answer questions to deploying agents that handle complex work across business units, use proprietary data and take actions on behalf of users. As models improve, agents find more uses and get more access. The more access an agent has, the more its company needs to control and check what it does.

8
00:01:28.577 --> 00:01:29.807
Protection in layers.

9
00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:51.895
Protection starts with safeguards inside the model. Managed Agents and NVIDIA Open Shell add limits that sit outside the model and apply to what the agent does. Each layer is designed to enforce its limits independently, so protection doesn't depend on any single layer. The layers are modular, so companies can adopt the ones that fit their setup.

10
00:01:52.695 --> 00:01:56.246
Claude Managed Agents does the work and holds the credentials.

11
00:01:56.696 --> 00:02:11.534
With Managed Agents, the agent loop runs on a separate server from the sandbox, the isolated environment where the work happens. Credentials, meaning passwords and access keys, are held in a separate vault, so the agent never sees them.

12
00:02:11.984 --> 00:02:25.593
Managed Agents also provides audit trails, which record what each agent did, and integration with a company's existing access controls. Companies can bring their own sandbox setup and choose where and how it runs.

13
00:02:26.393 --> 00:02:29.437
NVIDIA OpenShell sets what an agent can reach.

14
00:02:29.887 --> 00:02:51.690
OpenShell is open source secure runtime software from NVIDIA. It governs and monitors all A I agent behavior and enforces policies for every action. OpenShell blocks everything unless a rule allows it. It checks each tool an agent tries to use and applies rules to the files, network connections and data the agent accesses.

15
00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.886
The rules are enforced outside the agent, and OpenShell logs every decision it allows or blocks.

16
00:02:58.336 --> 00:03:13.790
Teams can start with narrow permissions, review the log, and use Claude to tighten the rules toward the least access a task needs. OpenShell's policy prover then uses mathematical proof to confirm what the agent can reach under the rules the team wrote.

17
00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.726
What Claude Managed Agents includes.

18
00:03:17.176 --> 00:03:23.626
Production-grade agents with secure sandboxing, authentication, and tool execution handled for you.

19
00:03:23.866 --> 00:03:31.418
Long-running sessions that operate autonomously for hours, with progress and outputs that persist even through disconnections.

20
00:03:31.658 --> 00:03:38.457
Multi-agent orchestration, where agents can spin up and direct other agents to parallelize complex work.

21
00:03:38.697 --> 00:03:47.081
Trusted governance, giving agents access to real systems with scoped permissions, identity management, and execution tracing built in.

22
00:03:47.881 --> 00:03:49.778
How teams use Managed Agents.

23
00:03:50.228 --> 00:04:05.471
Notion lets teams hand work to Claude inside their workspace. Engineers use it to ship code, and other employees use it to produce websites and presentations. Dozens of tasks can run in parallel while the team works on the results together.

24
00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:13.286
Rakuten runs specialist agents across engineering, product, sales, marketing, and finance, each deployed within a week.

25
00:04:13.526 --> 00:04:26.902
Asana built A I Teammates, agents that work alongside people in Asana projects, take on tasks and draft deliverables. Using Managed Agents, the team added advanced features faster than it could have otherwise.

26
00:04:27.702 --> 00:04:28.653
Availability.

27
00:04:29.103 --> 00:04:47.361
Managed Agents is available today. It can operate in a sandbox you control either running on your own infrastructure, or with a managed provider. NVIDIA OpenShell is open source under the Apache 2.0 license and available on GitHub and NVIDIA's developer resources page.

28
00:04:48.361 --> 00:05:06.449
That was Giving companies more control over their A I agents, with NVIDIA, from Claude Blog, published September 28, 2026. Read the original at claude dot com. This unofficial audio edition was generated automatically for the podcast Anthropic, Read Aloud.
